WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.270
Breaking news: a poll of one thousand
adults backs a new park plan.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.640
The country has millions of people.

3
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.730
A viewer scoffs: they never asked me!

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.830
Then two polls of one town disagree.

5
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.180
One asked five thousand
people on a sports website.

6
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.110
One asked a thousand, picked at
random from the electoral list.

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.920
Which should you trust?

8
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.530
In this mission, you'll
separate the population,

9
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.270
the whole group, from the
sample you actually ask.

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.350
You'll learn what random means: every
member has an equal chance of being chosen.

11
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.080
And you'll see how a sample can be biased,

12
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.430
like asking people at a gym
how often they exercise.

13
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: decide whether a thousand
people can speak for a whole country.
